WHY THE ROOT `LICENSE` FILE MOVES WHEN YOU SCAFFOLD
===================================================

A `LICENSE` file at a repository root is read as "this repository is under these
terms." That is correct for the template repo — it genuinely is GPL-2.0-or-later.
It is wrong for your company repo, whose main content is item 2 above.

So `/aios:company --create` moves the GPL text to `LICENSE-TEMPLATE` rather than
deleting it: the scaffolding you received stays licensed and attributed, while the
root of your repository stops asserting GPL over your business material. If your
company wants its own licence, add your own `LICENSE` — that slot is yours.

This split is the AIOS licence policy for company repos, recorded in the framework's
`LICENSE-AUDIT.md` § 4. It is a statement of how this template is shipped, not legal
advice; if the boundary matters commercially to you, have counsel look at it.
